                  {
                    "value": "9 \u00b7 NPV, IRR, Payback \u2014 from scratch",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontSize": "13pt"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": "A project is a trade: money out now for flows later. Discount every flow to today (block 6) and net against the cost: NPV = \u2212investment + \u03a3 CF\u209c/(1+hurdle)\u1d57. Positive means the flows repay the money AND its required return, with value left over.",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontSize": "9pt"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": "IRR asks the reverse question: at what rate r would this project only just break even (NPV = 0)? Found numerically by bisection. Compare IRR to the hurdle: above = pays more than capital costs.",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontSize": "9pt"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": "Payback = years until cumulative undiscounted flows cover the investment. It ignores the time value of money \u2014 which is exactly why it is only a tiebreaker, never the decision.",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontSize": "9pt"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": "\u2192 tab 5 \u00b7 Options, tests columns",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontSize": "9pt"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
